{
  "$comment": [
    "Every URL here is relative, and that is the whole trick. Manifest members resolve",
    "against the manifest's own URL, so `./` is the site root on the user site and the",
    "project subpath under PTK_BASE_PATH -- no build step has to rewrite this file, and a",
    "subpath deploy cannot ship a manifest whose start_url points at somebody else's root.",
    "Unknown members like this one are ignored by the manifest parser, which is what lets",
    "a JSON file carry the reasoning that a comment normally would.",
    "",
    "theme_color is the accent, matching the icon background, because it colours the",
    "system chrome around the installed app and the accent is the one colour that is",
    "recognisably this product in either scheme. background_color is the light surface: it",
    "paints the splash before any CSS loads, a manifest has exactly one of them, and a",
    "manifest cannot vary by prefers-color-scheme. The per-scheme values live in the",
    "documents as meta theme-color, which browsers do honour.",
    "",
    "orientation is \"any\" deliberately, and scripts/check-pwa.mjs fails the build if it",
    "stops being. An installed application takes its orientation from here, so \"portrait\"",
    "would override the device rotation lock for every visitor -- and the people that locks",
    "out are the ones who cannot rotate the phone back, which is exactly who WCAG 1.3.4 is",
    "written for. A lifter with the phone clamped to a rack is the same case arriving from",
    "the other side.",
    "",
    "There is deliberately no \"id\". It is the one member that does not resolve the way the",
    "rest of this file does: the algorithm parses it against the *origin* of the resolved",
    "start_url, so \"./\", \"foo\", \"/foo\" and \"../foo\" all mean the same thing and none of",
    "them can name a subpath. An \"id\" of \"./\" therefore claims the origin's root as this",
    "application's identity, which under PTK_BASE_PATH is a subpath deploy calling itself",
    "whatever else is installed from that host's root. Omitting it makes the identity",
    "default to the resolved start_url, which does carry the base -- the same property every",
    "other URL here has, obtained by leaving the member out rather than by writing one."
  ],
  "name": "Platform Toolkit",
  "short_name": "Toolkit",
  "description": "Open-source tools for the powerlifting community. Every tool works on its own and embeds anywhere.",
  "start_url": "./",
  "scope": "./",
  "display": "standalone",
  "orientation": "any",
  "theme_color": "#1f5fa8",
  "background_color": "#ffffff",
  "categories": ["sports", "utilities"],
  "lang": "en",
  "dir": "ltr",
  "icons": [
    {
      "src": "./icons/icon-192.png",
      "sizes": "192x192",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "src": "./icons/icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "any"
    },
    {
      "src": "./icons/icon-512.png",
      "sizes": "512x512",
      "type": "image/png",
      "purpose": "maskable"
    },
    {
      "src": "./icons/icon.svg",
      "sizes": "any",
      "type": "image/svg+xml",
      "purpose": "any"
    }
  ],
  "$comment_shortcuts": [
    "The long-press menu on the installed icon, and the only place the collection can be",
    "entered anywhere but the hub. There is still one application and one start_url -- a",
    "shortcut is a deep link into the running app, not a second installable thing -- which",
    "is why these are the four tools a lifter opens standing at a rack rather than all",
    "seven: a launcher shows about four and the ones past that are written for nobody.",
    "",
    "Every url is relative for the same reason start_url is, and a shortcut is the easiest",
    "member to get wrong here because an absolute one still works in development. No per",
    "shortcut icons: there is no per-tool artwork, and a launcher given nothing falls back",
    "to the application icon, which is honest. Naming the same file four times would put",
    "one indistinguishable barbell beside four different labels."
  ],
  "shortcuts": [
    {
      "name": "Training Logbook",
      "short_name": "Logbook",
      "description": "Plan a session and tick off each set as you finish it.",
      "url": "./logbook/"
    },
    {
      "name": "Warm-Up Calculator",
      "short_name": "Warm-Up",
      "description": "Warm-up sets and plate loading for a working weight.",
      "url": "./warm-up/"
    },
    {
      "name": "One-Rep Max Estimator",
      "short_name": "One-Rep Max",
      "description": "What a set you already did suggests about a single.",
      "url": "./one-rep-max/"
    },
    {
      "name": "Platform Targets",
      "short_name": "Targets",
      "description": "Classifications, records and qualification standards for one lifter.",
      "url": "./platform-targets/"
    }
  ],
  "$comment_screenshots": [
    "What a browser shows in place of a bare one-line install bar. Captured from the built",
    "site rather than drawn, so a stale one is a screenshot of a page that no longer looks",
    "like that and not a promise the product never kept.",
    "",
    "Two form factors because a browser picks by device and shows nothing at all when the",
    "set for the one it is on is empty: narrow is the phone, which is the device this",
    "collection is for, and wide is the desktop dialog. The narrow pair are the hub and the",
    "logbook -- the collection, then the one tool that works with no network, which is the",
    "reason to install rather than bookmark.",
    "",
    "Deliberately not precached. These are shown by the browser's own install UI before",
    "there is an installed application, and a phone that has one will never ask for them",
    "again -- putting a third of a megabyte of imagery on the device at install time is the",
    "same mistake as precaching the record books."
  ],
  "screenshots": [
    {
      "src": "./screenshots/hub-narrow.png",
      "sizes": "720x1280",
      "type": "image/png",
      "form_factor": "narrow",
      "label": "The list of tools in the collection, on a phone."
    },
    {
      "src": "./screenshots/logbook-narrow.png",
      "sizes": "720x1280",
      "type": "image/png",
      "form_factor": "narrow",
      "label": "The training logbook, ready to plan a session, on a phone."
    },
    {
      "src": "./screenshots/hub-wide.png",
      "sizes": "1280x720",
      "type": "image/png",
      "form_factor": "wide",
      "label": "The list of tools in the collection, on a desktop browser."
    }
  ]
}
